      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-284103",
      ":question/problem": "A bakery is purchasing bags of flour and sugar from its supplier. The delivery truck can carry no more than $250$ pounds in a single shipment. Each bag of flour weighs $4.5$ pounds, and each bag of sugar weighs $6.8$ pounds. The bakery also wants to buy at least three times as many bags of flour as bags of sugar. Let $f$ represent the number of bags of flour and $s$ represent the number of bags of sugar, where $f$ and $s$ are nonnegative integers. Which of the following systems of inequalities best represents this situation?"
    },
