      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-287179",
      ":question/problem": "A company is packing laptops and monitors into shipping crates. Each crate can carry no more than $180$ pounds. Each laptop weighs $5.2$ pounds, and each monitor weighs $12.3$ pounds. The number of monitors must be no more than twice the number of laptops. Let $l$ represent the number of laptops and $m$ represent the number of monitors, where $l$ and $m$ are nonnegative integers. Which of the following systems of inequalities best represents this situation?"
